00:22:23.330 --> 00:22:26.800
Today we're making a peppery steak

00:22:26.800 --> 00:22:28.710
with an agrodolce sauce.

00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:29.543
- Let's do it.

00:22:29.543 --> 00:22:30.376
(audience cheers)
(audience applauds)

00:22:30.376 --> 00:22:33.450
- So we're gonna start with
this New York strip over here.

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:34.520
For this recipe,

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:36.585
the reason why I love a New York strip

00:22:36.585 --> 00:22:40.040
is because it's tender like a filet

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:43.470
and it has the flavor and
fat, just like a ribeye.

00:22:43.470 --> 00:22:44.900
So the first thing we're gonna do

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:48.550
is season up the steak
really, really well.

00:22:48.550 --> 00:22:52.130
And then you park that for
like an hour and let it sit.

00:22:52.130 --> 00:22:55.020
We have some freshly
crushed black pepper corns.

00:22:55.020 --> 00:22:57.740
You can lay that on your plate or on top,

00:22:57.740 --> 00:23:01.160
and you're gonna press down to adhere.

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:03.790
So we've seasoned off both sides.

00:23:03.790 --> 00:23:07.350
And meanwhile, you want your pan heating

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:09.730
over medium to medium high heat.

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:11.540
When your pan is nice and hot,

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:13.490
you're gonna add some oil.

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:14.690
And right here, actually,

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:17.810
we have a steak that has been searing.

00:23:17.810 --> 00:23:19.310
So it's nice and hot.

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:20.320
- Time to turn it over?

00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:23.157
- Yeah, I like to, oh, look at that.

00:23:23.157 --> 00:23:25.610
Beautiful.
(audience cheers)

00:23:25.610 --> 00:23:30.610
So this recipe is gonna cook
stove top for six minutes,

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:33.200
but just make sure
you're doing essentially

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:35.710
the same amount of time on both sides.

00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:37.110
- [Drew] Same amount
of time on both sides.

00:23:37.110 --> 00:23:40.470
- And we're gonna finish
this steak in the oven.

00:23:40.470 --> 00:23:42.090
- Okay.
- That's the clue.

00:23:42.090 --> 00:23:44.690
One thing to look for when you're going

00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:48.050
into the oven is definitely
use an oven thermometer.

00:23:48.050 --> 00:23:49.890
So we're gonna make the
agrodolce sauce real quick.

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:50.723
- [Drew] Let's do it.

00:23:50.723 --> 00:23:52.393
- We're gonna dump everything in,

00:23:52.393 --> 00:23:54.560
that's two tablespoons of shallots,

00:23:54.560 --> 00:23:56.300
- Two tablespoons shallots.

00:23:56.300 --> 00:23:58.940
- All of that roughly chopped cranberries.

00:23:58.940 --> 00:24:00.330
Wonderful food.

00:24:00.330 --> 00:24:03.970
And then that is my balsamic over there.

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:04.803
Some water,

00:24:04.803 --> 00:24:06.290
and then we're gonna do some honey.

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:08.620
So all you have to do
is basically bring this

00:24:08.620 --> 00:24:10.440
to a boil and then simmer it

00:24:10.440 --> 00:24:14.310
for four minutes until
it's nice and thick.

00:24:14.310 --> 00:24:17.820
And the last little thing is off the heat,

00:24:17.820 --> 00:24:21.320
we're gonna pour in our mustard.

00:24:21.320 --> 00:24:23.560
So we actually, on the side, Drew,

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:26.800
have a steak, beautiful
steak that has been resting,

00:24:26.800 --> 00:24:28.670
critical piece to cooking steak,

00:24:28.670 --> 00:24:31.650
rest your meat for at least 10 minutes.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:34.070
So the last thing to do is just spoon

00:24:34.070 --> 00:24:35.893
some of that beautiful sauce on.

00:24:37.660 --> 00:24:39.460
- Oh, this cut's, wow,

00:24:39.460 --> 00:24:41.660
- I guess you just gotta take a taste.

00:24:41.660 --> 00:24:42.493
- I'm sorry.

00:24:44.261 --> 00:24:45.263
I don't, I just eat.

00:24:46.700 --> 00:24:49.480
It is really, really good.

00:24:49.480 --> 00:24:54.250
For today a quinoa risotto
with winter squash,

00:24:54.250 --> 00:24:56.873
seared mushrooms and fresh
herbs, shall we jump in?

00:24:56.873 --> 00:24:58.000
- Yes, we shall.

00:24:58.000 --> 00:24:59.450
- So the first thing you're gonna do

00:24:59.450 --> 00:25:01.690
is actually roast your squash.

00:25:01.690 --> 00:25:05.235
- And you're gonna roast them
at like 400 for about 20?

00:25:05.235 --> 00:25:06.360
- 20 to 30.

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:08.500
What I like to do is
actually cut the squash

00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:11.230
into chunks like this,
drizzle some olive oil,

00:25:11.230 --> 00:25:15.860
salt, and pepper, stick it in
the oven, 20 to 30, let it go.

00:25:15.860 --> 00:25:17.790
And then you're gonna take it out

00:25:17.790 --> 00:25:20.170
and we're actually gonna make a puree.

